  "rules": {
    "summary": "2026-27: 18 clubs, 34 rounds (8 August 2026 to 21 May 2027). The top two are promoted to Ligue 1; 3rd, 4th and 5th play the play-offs (5th at 4th, the winner at 3rd, each a single match), whose winner meets Ligue 1's 16th over two legs. The bottom two go down to Ligue 3, and 16th plays the Ligue 3 play-off winner over two legs. Teams level on points are ranked by goal difference, then head-to-head points and goal difference (only once both meetings are played), then goals scored, wins, away wins, discipline (1 point a yellow card, 3 a red) and lots.",
    "sources": [
      "https://www.lfp.fr/assets/26_27_Reglement_Competitions_08_09_2026_45d0881157.pdf",
      "https://ligue1.com/fr/competitions/ligue2bkt/standings"
    ]
  },
  "notes": [
    "There is no earlier Ligue 2 season in the feed to backtest on. With the previous season removed, eight other leagues' 2023-24 to 2025-26 week-ahead predictions scored 0.194-0.222 (ranked probability score) against 0.229-0.235 for home/draw/away base rates, 0.002-0.008 worse than with it. This season's first 63 Ligue 2 matches scored 0.234 against 0.221 for base rates, so treat early match predictions with care.",
    "Away wins are the last tiebreak step modelled; the league then compares disciplinary points, which the feed does not have, and the table falls back to club names."
  ],
